{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Speak to all the congregation of Israel.</b> For all are obligated in commandments." "<b>And they shall take for themselves.</b> One who has [livestock] from his flock, for they had abundant flock, or they may buy. And Yefet said that from the tenth day they began to prepare the lamb, fourteen days, but we do not know whether this is a commandment for the generations or [applies only] to the Passover of Egypt." "A lamb for a father's house. If they are few." "<b>A lamb for a house.</b> If they are many. And after he said 'a lamb for a father's house,' he said 'a lamb for every house,' and at the beginning of this book I explained 'house.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:26.254298219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}